From: fedora-opd2413 <noreply@local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: do not reset mux to USB mode while partner is in alt-mode

When a Type-C dock or monitor with both USB data and DisplayPort Alt
Mode finishes PD Alt Mode negotiation, the PPM delivers a
UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_CHANGE event with both UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_FLAG_USB
and UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE set.

On Qualcomm PMIC GLINK platforms, pmic_glink_altmode manages the
DisplayPort Alt Mode pin assignment on the shared Type-C mux
(wcd939x-usbss SBU/AUX crossbar and QMP USB3/DP combo PHY). In
ucsi_partner_change(), checking only PARTNER_FLAG_USB causes UCSI to
unconditionally call typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB)
(svid=0, mode=1) right after pmic_glink_altmode configures DP Alt Mode
(mode=4/5, svid=0xff01):
- wcd939x-usbss physically disconnects SBU1/SBU2 (DP AUX) and briefly
  blanks D+/D- switches (-EPROTO -71 on USB2 enumeration).
- phy-qcom-qmp-combo resets and tears down the combo PHY back to
  QMPPHY_MODE_USB3_ONLY, breaking HDMI/DP Alt Mode and dropping the
  USB 3.2 SuperSpeed hub link.

Skip typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB) when
UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE is set. Plain USB attachments,
audio/debug accessories, USB role switching, alt-mode exit back to
USB-only, and disconnect (TYPEC_STATE_SAFE) remain unchanged.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index 6f11d1e48..7c8d9e0f1 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1356,7 +1356,8 @@ static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_MODE_AUDIO);
 			break;
 		default:
-			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB))
+			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB) &&
+			    !UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE))
 				typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB);
 		}
 
